Add **Hermes Personal Task Manager @VERSION@** as a community plugin in the tools
category. It records personal tasks, one level of subtasks, notes and confirmed
results in one profile-scoped SQLite database shared by chat tools, Dashboard
and Desktop/WebApp. It does not execute tasks.

Pinned source: https://github.com/RudiFreeman/hermes-personal-task-manager/tree/@SHA@

## Surfaces and behavior

- Three native tools: personal_tasks_list, personal_tasks_add and personal_tasks_update.
- Dashboard manifest/API and native host React components.
- Desktop SDK route/sidebar, ctx.rest and lifecycle cleanup. No core overrides,
  raw native bridge, remote executable imports or self-updater.
- English-first UI and documentation, optional Russian translation.
- Explicit parent completion atomically completes active children; reopening
  preserves child completion. Trash is restorable; purge requires confirmation.
- Hermes tool instructions require explicit user requests and completion evidence;
  revisions prevent stale writes. The evidence text is not independently audited.

## Disclosures (catalog rule 13)

- Storage: task titles/descriptions, completion timestamps, notes, revisions and
  events in the active profile's plugin data directory. No credentials stored.
- Network: authenticated requests only to the current Hermes instance's plugin
  API. No third-party runtime service, telemetry, fonts or CDN. README badges
  request static images from shields.io when a Markdown client renders them.
- Outside data: no normal runtime reads outside the plugin's source/data. The
  optional, non-secret PTM_DATA_DIR development override chooses another storage
  directory and must not be shared across profiles accidentally.
- Execution: no shell commands, task executors, background workers, scheduled
  jobs, token refresh, credential-store access or approval bypass. Visible UI
  polls every three seconds; timers/listeners are removed on unload.
- Optional development preview binds loopback and generates an in-memory token.
  Optional browser checks read operator-supplied authentication-state files;
  these test files are not loaded by the runtime or shipped with credentials.
- Schema 1 migrates atomically to 2. Upgrade all writers together and back up the
  stopped database plus WAL first; older plugin versions refuse schema 2.
- Prebuilt readable JavaScript is committed with sources/build script/lockfile.
  Host surfaces use host React; preview includes React under the notices in
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. No bundled native executable or Python bytecode.

